      "topic": "Identifying conics",
      "source": "TN HSE Mar 2024",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 1,
      "q": "The type of conic section for $x^2-3=5x+3y$ is :",
      "options": [
        "hyperbola",
        "ellipse",
        "circle",
        "parabola"
      ],
      "answer": 3,
      "solution": "Only $x^2$ appears (no $y^2$, no $xy$): $x^2=5x+3y+3$ is a **parabola**."
    },
    {
      "id": "tn12m-con-23q5",
      "chapter": "Two Dimensional Analytical Geometry II",
      "topic": "Parabola",
      "source": "TN HSE Mar 2023",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 1,
      "q": "The number of normals that can be drawn from a point to the parabola $y^2=4ax$ is :",
      "options": [
        "3",
        "2",
        "0",
        "1"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "solution": "The normal at $(at^2,2at)$ is $y+tx=2at+at^3$ — a cubic in $t$, so at most **3** normals pass through a point."
    },
    {
