      "source": "TN HSE Mar 2025",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 1,
      "q": "An ellipse has $OB$ as semi minor axes, $F$ and $F'$ its foci and the angle $FBF'$ is a right angle. Then the eccentricity of the ellipse is :",
      "options": [
        "$\\dfrac14$",
        "$\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt2}$",
        "$\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt3}$",
        "$\\dfrac12$"
      ],
      "answer": 1,
      "solution": "$\\angle FBF'=90^\\circ$ makes $\\angle OBF=45^\\circ$, so $OF=OB$: $ae=b$. Then $a^2e^2=a^2(1-e^2)$, $e^2=\\dfrac12$, $e=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt2}$."
    },
    {
      "id": "tn12m-con-01",
      "chapter": "Two Dimensional Analytical Geometry II",
      "topic": "Hyperbola",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 1,
      "q": "The eccentricity of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{x^2}{16}-\\dfrac{y^2}{9}=1$ is :",
      "options": [
        "$\\dfrac54$",
        "$\\dfrac45$",
        "$\\dfrac53$",
        "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt7}{4}$"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "solution": "$e=\\sqrt{1+\\dfrac{b^2}{a^2}}=\\sqrt{1+\\dfrac{9}{16}}=\\dfrac54$."
