    {
      "id": "tn12m-con-11",
      "chapter": "Two Dimensional Analytical Geometry II",
      "topic": "Parabola",
      "type": "long",
      "marks": 5,
      "q": "Find the vertex, focus, equation of the directrix and length of the latus rectum of the parabola $y^2-4y-8x+12=0$.",
      "solution": "Complete the square: $y^2-4y+4=8x-8$, i.e. $(y-2)^2=8(x-1)$.\n\nThis is $Y^2=4aX$ with $X=x-1$, $Y=y-2$ and $4a=8$, so $a=2$.\n\n**Vertex** $(1,2)$.\n\n**Focus** $(1+a,2)=(3,2)$.\n\n**Directrix** $x=1-a$, i.e. $x=-1$.\n\n**Latus rectum** $4a=8$."
    }
